# React Components Instructions

When working in React component or page files:

- Use TypeScript with explicit prop interfaces
- Use named exports for components, default exports only for pages
- Keep components under 150 lines — extract sub-components if longer
- Use {{stack.frontend.styling}} for all styling
{{#if (eq stack.frontend.state_management "tanstack-query")}}
- Use TanStack Query hooks for data fetching (never raw fetch in components)
{{/if}}
- Add aria labels and alt text for accessibility
- Handle loading, error, and empty states in every data-dependent component
- Extract reusable logic into custom hooks in `hooks/` directory
